00:24:27.101 --> 00:24:30.250
that this one was, someone
asked you this during an event.

00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:31.000
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:34.110
So I was in an
event, and someone

00:24:34.110 --> 00:24:36.740
was chatting to me about
building custom schedulers

00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:39.220
within Kubernetes, and how
they could get involved

00:24:39.220 --> 00:24:40.760
with that whole aspect of it.

00:24:40.760 --> 00:24:43.240
And at the time, I wasn't
quite sure where to send them.

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:45.960
So I ended up having
to do some research.

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:47.680
So I basically
hunted around, and I

00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:50.550
realized that Kubernetes
has a series of what's

00:24:50.550 --> 00:24:53.130
called special interest
groups, or SIGs,

00:24:53.130 --> 00:24:57.530
that, basically, cover each
different aspect of Kubernetes.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:25:00.000
So there's one for scheduling,
there's one for network,

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.810
there's one for
scalability, and there's

00:25:02.810 --> 00:25:05.097
one for storage, et cetera.

00:25:05.097 --> 00:25:05.930
They're really cool.

00:25:05.930 --> 00:25:07.471
They've got people
who run them, they

00:25:07.471 --> 00:25:09.970
have regular
meetings that happen,

00:25:09.970 --> 00:25:12.965
they have Slack channels
dedicated specifically to them.

00:25:12.965 --> 00:25:14.590
So if it's something
that you're, like,

00:25:14.590 --> 00:25:15.820
oh, I really want
to get involved

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:17.840
with how Kubernetes orders
scales, for example,

00:25:17.840 --> 00:25:20.600
or, I really want to dig into
this side of the open source

00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:24.050
project, it's a really easy
way to find the right pathway,

00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:26.880
the right people to talk to,
and the Google group to get on.

00:25:26.880 --> 00:25:27.940
We'll have a link
in the show notes.

00:25:27.940 --> 00:25:30.090
It's just a whole page with
[? markdown ?] inside GitHub

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:32.650
that lists all of these so that
you can get involved really,

00:25:32.650 --> 00:25:33.640
really easily.

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:34.556
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

